`ffi_lib "m"` names a library Debian-style glibc does not ship in
loadable form. `FFI.map_library_name("m")` is `libm.so` (the gem's own
rule), and there `/usr/lib/<triple>/libm.so` is a 149-byte LINKER SCRIPT
out of the -dev package -- `dlopen` refuses it. The loadable file is the
soname `libm.so.6`, which no spelling in the gem's mapping produces.
macOS has a real `libm.dylib`, so the `.expected` blessed there runs.

CRuby with the ffi gem fails the same way on the same host, so this is
the platform's library layout rather than zeo's resolution. The bare
name `c` is the one exception, and it IS handled: the gem maps it to
`Platform::LIBC`, which zeo's runtime answers with `libc.so.6` (see
`dlopen_first`).
